# Rule 50 — boundary-governed-function (ADR 0028: the automation boundary).
#
# The automation boundary concept id, `AUTON-BOUNDARY`, is fixed by ADR 0028 (its per-coverage-area
# partition by ADR 0029) — it is not a configuration value, so it is named directly here, the same way
# the consumer's linter's `_boundary_governed_functions` helper (`[overlay] linter_script`) reads it off
# `terms["AUTON-BOUNDARY"]`. That helper's actual test is "the target id starts with FUNC-";
# `?func a itpra:FUNCTION` is the graph-native equivalent (FUNC-<slug> is, by the id convention in
# schema.yaml, always type Function) — so this rule reproduces the same set the linter reports, one hop,
# directly, with no reasoner. `AUTON-BOUNDARY` also governs the delegated-actor concept `AUTON-ACTOR`,
# which is excluded here because it is not a Function.
#
# The PREFIX block (itpra:, itpra-o:, itpra-g:) is prepended at run time from `itpra-onto.toml`
# `[iri]` (ADR 0004) — this file names no base IRI and declares no PREFIX itself.

CONSTRUCT {
  ?func a itpra-o:BoundaryGovernedFunction .
}
WHERE {
  GRAPH itpra-g:t1 {
    itpra:AUTON-BOUNDARY itpra-o:governs ?func .
    ?func a itpra:FUNCTION .
  }
}
